# Articles from three OpenEdition journals: Revue francaise des sciences de
# l'information et de la communication, Questions de communication, and Terrain.
# Academic French, and the reason this corpus is here is that OpenEdition sets it
# properly: guillemets carry a real no-break space, apostrophes are U+2019, and
# there is not a straight double quote in the sample that was probed. That is
# what makes every finding over it a suspected false positive rather than a
# recall test.
#
# Three journals rather than one so that a single copy editor's habits do not
# stand in for published French. Anthropology sits beside communication studies
# for the same reason the Spanish corpora span a gazette, an FAQ and a language
# foundation: one register is not a language.
#
# Identifiers came from the OpenEdition OAI-PMH endpoint and each URL was fetched
# once before it was frozen here, so none of them 404s on the next person to run
# `pnpm corpus`.
# Frozen 2026-08-10. format: html
#
# A second column is an Internet Archive capture: fixed bytes, so a rebuild
# reproduces instead of resampling. A URL without one is fetched live, and
# `--live` ignores the column entirely. gates/README.md has the coverage.
